# Fake privacy rules. Copy to ~/.claude/.journal-redact, then edit.
# Keep real policy out of Git.
# Shared core uses rules before model, temp file, save and Git upload.
# Missing policy uses builtins only. Public publish needs policy file.
# Bad regex or unreadable policy blocks flow.
# Order matters. Specific names first. Replacement must not match any rule.
# Literal => replacement. Bare literal becomes <redacted>.
# re:pattern => replacement uses Python regex. Case ignored.

acme-api-gateway => internal-api-gateway
registry.acme.internal => internal-registry
re:PROJ-\d+ => <ticket>
AcmeCorp => internal-org
